TweetNaCl — https://tweetnacl.cr.yp.to/

Public domain. From the authors (Daniel J. Bernstein, Bernard van Gaans,
Tanja Lange, Peter Schwabe):

    TweetNaCl is a self-contained public-domain C library, so you can
    simply add tweetnacl.c and tweetnacl.h to your project.

Vendored here (gframe/tweetnacl/tweetnacl.c, tweetnacl.h) verbatim from the
2014-04-27 release. Used for Ed25519 signature verification of the signed
banlist artifact (gframe/banlist_verify.cpp) — this client never signs and
never generates a keypair.

gframe/tweetnacl/randombytes.c is this project's own code (same license as
the rest of the fork), not part of the vendored library: it exists only to
satisfy a linker reference TweetNaCl declares but this client never calls.
